<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Le Temps des cerises</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Le Temps des cerises&quot; (&quot;The Time of Cherries&quot;) is a French song written in 1866, with words by Jean-Baptiste Clément and music by Antoine Renard. It became very well known throughout the French-speaking countries. The song came to be closely linked with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris-commune">Paris Commune</a>.</p></div>
